# The corpus images are FROM scratch and copy one directory; the tools image
# copies nothing at all. Everything else in the tree is build input that has
# already been consumed by `make corpus`, so keeping it out of the context is
# what makes the build a copy rather than a build.
*
!output
!output-compact
# core.db's directory, for the corpus-db image. An allowlist entry is exact:
# "!output" does not readmit "output-db", so a tree left out here reaches the
# COPY as nothing at all rather than as an error.
!output-db
